#
# This registers GcpSecretsTemplateVariableProvider as a bean in the gateway's MAIN application
# context, which is the only reason it is ever discovered.
#
# The obvious-looking key, `io.gravitee.el.TemplateVariableProvider`, is DEAD in APIM 4.12.12:
# nothing reads it. The one declaration of it in the gateway (gravitee-apim-gateway-reactor) is
# vestigial — NodeTemplateVariableProvider actually becomes a bean through an @Bean method in
# ReactorConfiguration, and it has a two-argument constructor no factories loader could satisfy.
# Declaring our provider under that key gets it silently ignored.
#
# The keys that ARE read by a SpringFactoriesLoader that registers beans:
#   io.gravitee.plugin.core.api.PluginHandler       -> main context   (used here)
#   io.gravitee.node.container.ContainerInitializer -> boot context
#
# PluginHandler is chosen because the main context is where the EL machinery lives; the boot context
# holds only Configuration/Environment and the secret plugin manager. We are not really a plugin
# handler — canHandle() returns false — the interface is purely the registration hook.
#
io.gravitee.plugin.core.api.PluginHandler=\
    io.fluenthealth.gravitee.secretprovider.gcp.el.GcpSecretsTemplateVariableProvider
